<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Said bin Taimur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1910–1972</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Said bin Taimur was sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscat">Muscat</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> from 1932 to 1970. He kept the country isolated and frugal, won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jebel-akhdar-war">Jebel Akhdar War</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imamate">Imamate</a> of Oman with British help and sold <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gwadar">Gwadar</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> in 1958. Even after oil exports began in 1967 development stayed slow, and his son Qaboos deposed him in 1970.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/said-bin-taimur.jpg" alt="Said bin Taimur" width="320" height="465" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: British Library: India Office Records and Private Papers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Said_Bin_Timur.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
